// SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0
; specs/turbobaby/deeplink.t27 -- the link grammar that decides where a customer lands.
; This contract owns four things and nothing else: the shape of a Telegram `start` payload
; (length, character class, attribution segment), the four-stage pipeline that carries one from a
; share button to a screen and what each stage may and may not do, the rule that an unparseable
; payload fails to a NAMED screen rather than a guessed one, and the compatibility set -- the
; payload shapes and route aliases kept resolvable because links already sit in customers'
; Telegram histories. It owns no product id, no price, no catalog row, no status code and no
; translated string. ASCII only (L3), English only (LANG-EN).
; --
; WHY (measured 2026-09-21). `grep -ril deeplink specs/` over the twenty contracts that existed
; before this one returns ZERO files, and `grep -rl startapp specs/` returns zero as well. The
; corpus says what the product answers, what it charges and who is asking, and not one line of it
; says how a customer ARRIVES. That silence is expensive here, because the arrival path is the one
; surface in this repository whose two halves cannot see each other: `src/ui` is
; `#[cfg(target_arch = "wasm32")]` (src/trios/deeplink.rs:14), so `cargo test --lib` on the host
; reaches neither the parser wiring nor the landing table, and stages 2 and 4 of the pipeline were
; written twice with no way to compare them (src/trios/deeplink.rs:12-18). The measured cost of
; that invisibility is on the record: the bot's prefix list and the app's disagreed about TWELVE
; payloads out of a forty-six-payload sweep (src/bot/mod.rs:190-193), in both directions -- links
; the app could open that the bot refused to answer, and links the bot answered with a button the
; app could not parse. Both read to a customer as one thing: you tap, and nothing happens.
; --
; WHY IT IS STILL OPEN (measured 2026-09-21). The repair put one vocabulary in
; `src/trios/deeplink.rs` and the classifier now delegates to the parser (src/bot/mod.rs:209,
; src/trios/deeplink.rs:264-265), so stages 2 and 4 can no longer disagree about WHETHER a payload
; is answerable. They can still disagree about WHERE it lands, and today they do. FIVE targets are
; declared (src/trios/deeplink.rs:75-103) and FOUR of them have a landing branch in the app:
; reorder, cart, product and order, at src/ui/app.rs:175, :183, :230 and :239, consumed by
; src/ui/screens/home_screen.rs:177-204. The fifth, `Referrals`, has none. `parse_start_param`
; answers None for every non-product target (src/ui/share.rs:105-121, the `_` arm at :119) and no
; other reader exists: `grep -rn "Target::Referrals" src/` returns eleven hits, ten inside
; `src/trios/deeplink.rs` itself and one comment at src/notification_queue.rs:174 (was :113; the 2026-09-21 drain rewrite moved it, the comment is unchanged; re-pinned 2026-09-26, when the held-kinds guard moved it 16 lines and the base's :157 was found one line short of it). So the payload a
; live notification button sends (src/notification_queue.rs:177-180, was :116-119 and then :161-164, one per friend-joined,
; friend-ordered and milestone message) is classified as answerable, the bot renders a Mini App
; button for it (src/bot/commands.rs:232-252), the app sets no signal, and the customer lands on
; the application root. That is precisely the shape the file itself condemns at
; src/trios/deeplink.rs:283-285 and the shape the retired `Garden` target shipped in
; (src/trios/deeplink.rs:231-237): a resolver, an event, and no navigation.
; --
; WHERE THE BRIEF IS REFUTED. The brief cites src/ui/routes.rs:128-155 for "the startapp grammar
; and the legacy targets it still resolves". Half of that is wrong. Those lines are the doc
; comments and bodies of exactly TWO compatibility aliases, `Sets` (:128-140) and `Sommelier`
; (:142-155); the third alias, `/skate`, is not in that window at all -- its route attribute is at
; :68-71 and its component at :275-282. No grammar of any kind appears in src/ui/routes.rs: the
; length cap and the character class are declared at src/trios/deeplink.rs:24-28 and enforced by
; the two predicates at :106-112 and :115-120. A reader who opened :128-155 expecting a grammar
; would find three sentences about an empty `/api/sets` response and leave with no cap, no
; character class and no separator convention.
; --
; A SECOND CORRECTION, AND IT WEAKENS A GUARANTEE. src/trios/deeplink.rs:242-256 `destination` is
; described in its own doc comment as where a target is supposed to land the customer, and it is
; gated: the test at :288-334 asserts that every target names a screen that is not the home
; screen, and that each of the five product kinds gets its OWN screen. `grep -rn "destination("
; src/` returns five hits and ALL FIVE are inside `src/trios/deeplink.rs` -- the definition at
; :242 and four call sites at :291, :305, :321 and :663, every one of them inside
; `#[cfg(test)] mod tests`. The table has no production caller. What actually places a customer is
; `ProductKind::route` at src/ui/share.rs:87-91, whose single caller is
; src/ui/screens/home_screen.rs:181, and it sends ALL FIVE product kinds to one destination
; (src/ui/share.rs:70-86 records that as deliberate, dated 2026-09-16, because the per-kind screens
; are retired and an empty grid is a dead end). So the gated table separates five kinds, the
; shipped table collapses them, the two do not agree, and no test can notice: one lives where
; `cargo test` runs and the other lives behind the wasm gate. This contract states the SHAPE of
; the landing rule and refuses to declare which screen any kind lands on, because that fact has
; two live answers in one repository and picking either would be a false guarantee.
; --
; WHAT THIS FILE NEVER DOES. It contains no URL fixture, no bot username, and no product,
; order or unit id: a payload example here is a shape with a bracketed placeholder, never a value.
; It invents no analytics parameter -- the only attribution the wire carries is the trailing
; `__<source>` segment already built and read by src/trios/deeplink.rs:132-137 and :157-162, and
; its reporting hop at src/ui/app.rs:203-229 belongs to the app, not to this grammar. It declares
; no product price and no catalog field; a shared card's money is loaded server-side from the
; database and never from the caller (src/api/share.rs:15-17), and the link itself carries a kind
; prefix and an id and nothing more (src/api/share.rs:220-227). It restates no retirement
; decision: WHY a dead path is kept alive is REUSES_LEGACY_RETIREMENT_ID's subject and arrives
; here as the abstract boolean `retirement_keeps_the_route`. It restates no identity check: a
; resolved link is not a proof and REUSES_REQUEST_IDENTITY_ID owns what one is. It restates no
; locale set, fallback or key: REUSES_LOCALE_POLICY_ID owns those, and this file records only the
; measured fact that the payload grammar has no locale segment. The word "skate" appears here as a
; ROUTE alias; turbobaby/star-award owns it as RETAINED_LEGACY_SOURCE, a retained score-source
; string, and the two are
; different subjects that share a syllable. No renter name, handle, phone, key code, plate, debt,
; cost or personal note appears in any constant, fixture or comment (D14) -- and that prohibition
; has a measured origin in this very grammar, recorded below.
; phi^2 + 1/phi^2 = 3 | TRINITY

module turbobaby-deeplink;

pub const KIND : str = "contract";
pub const ID : str = "turbobaby/deeplink";
pub const NAME : str = "TurboBaby deep-link grammar and landing";
pub const WORLD : str = "gHashTag/turbobaby-user-bot";
pub const SOURCE : str = "src/trios/deeplink.rs";
pub const MEASURED_AT : str = "2026-09-21";
pub const DECISIONS : [3]str = ["D5", "D14", "D19"];

