; contracts then present. Neither the mechanism nor its vocabulary had an owner.
;
; THE ZERO IS DATED, AND IT HAS ALREADY MOVED -- TWICE. Re-running `grep -ril deeplink specs/` at
; the end of the same session printed THREE paths, one of them this file, and that reading of 2
; others is kept below as the wave reading. It is no longer current. RE-MEASURED 2026-09-21
; against the finished 43-file corpus the same command prints EIGHT paths: SEVEN others plus this
; file. A reader who runs the command today and reads 8 has not refuted the zero -- the zero is
; scoped to the twenty contracts that existed first, which is why the size of the corpus it was
; taken over is declared beside it rather than left implicit, and why the later counts carry
; dates of their own. The second grep has NOT moved: `grep -rl startapp specs/` still prints one
; path, this file, and zero others, re-run 2026-09-21. That one is a real standing absence and is
; the only one this file still claims as such.
pub const CONTRACTS_BEFORE_THIS_ONE : u8 = 20;
pub const CONTRACTS_MENTIONING_DEEPLINK : u8 = 0;
pub const CONTRACTS_MENTIONING_STARTAPP : u8 = 0;
; Contracts OTHER THAN THIS ONE that the command finds; the command itself prints one more.
; The first figure is the WAVE reading and is superseded by the dated one under it.
pub const CONTRACTS_MENTIONING_DEEPLINK_AFTER_THIS_WAVE : u8 = 2;
pub const CORPUS_FILE_COUNT : u8 = 43;
pub const CORPUS_FILES_OTHER_THAN_THIS_ONE : u8 = 42;
pub const CONTRACTS_MENTIONING_DEEPLINK_2026_09_21 : u8 = 7;
pub const CONTRACTS_MENTIONING_STARTAPP_2026_09_21 : u8 = 0;
pub const THE_STARTAPP_ZERO_STILL_HOLDS : bool = true;
pub const ZERO_GREP_COMMANDS : [2]str = ["grep -ril deeplink specs/", "grep -rl startapp specs/"];
; Re-measured 2026-09-22 and deliberately NOT bound: a census of the corpus moves with every new
; contract. The 43 and 42 above are KEPT as the 2026-09-21 reading and the denominator of the
; 2026_09_21 counts. "The finished 43-file corpus" was not finished: 14b01ac added
; order_presentation.t27 and person_naming.t27 later on 2026-09-21, and specs/ holds 45 tracked
; .t27 files. Both commands re-run at a33e500 over the 45: `grep -ril deeplink specs/` prints NINE
; paths, EIGHT others plus this file -- the new one is turbobaby/order-presentation, which declares
; the deeplink edge by ID -- and `grep -rl startapp specs/` still prints one path, this file.
pub const CORPUS_FILE_COUNT_REMEASURED : u8 = 45;
pub const CORPUS_FILES_OTHER_THAN_THIS_ONE_REMEASURED : u8 = 44;
pub const CORPUS_FILE_COUNT_REMEASURED_AT : str = "2026-09-22";
